# Binding documents (read before working)

Gurukul has three binding documents. Where code and spec disagree, **the spec
wins and the code is the bug**.

1. `docs/locked-decisions.md` — the product spec. Where code and spec disagree,
   the spec wins and the code is the bug.
2. `docs/gurukul-spec-rules.md` — **rules 1–32, binding.** Read in full before
   working. (Was omitted from an earlier version of this rule only because it
   appeared absent on a stale checkout at tip `7c8b435`; it is present from
   `4ee4dae` onward.)
3. `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` (repo root) — deferred work / known findings.
   Note: it contains **two sections numbered 8**; both are real, not a typo.

## Branch

Live work is `claude/gurukul-s10-cold-start-96242c`.

**NOT `claude/threshold-rulings-schema-f179b7`**, which this rule named until
2026-09-08 and which is now 13+ commits behind. Three sessions ran against that
stale tip and produced figures that looked plausible; a fourth stopped only
because a file it expected was missing. `main`'s tip is worse still — it lacks
`KNOWN_ISSUES.md`, `docs/gurukul-spec-rules.md` and the
`verify:caller-privileges` script, so gates pass there meaninglessly.

Confirm the branch before running any gate, and confirm the numbers too. On the
live tip expect **167 caller-privileges assertions** and **618 tests / 56 files**.
Seeing 129, 158, 571 or 613 means an older tip — stop rather than report from it.

`npm run check:pushed` (rule 32) fails if HEAD is ahead of or behind origin, and
runs first in `npm run preflight`.

## A document this rule does NOT list

`docs/GURUKUL-V1.md` has been cited to sessions as the canonical v1 description
and as the first thing to read. **It exists in no ref**, local or remote —
searched exhaustively on 2026-09-07 and again on 2026-09-08. It is not a stale
checkout. Until someone pushes it, the three documents above are the binding set,
and v1 scope must not be inferred from anything else.
